This extension adds Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]MicroPatches automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][size=3][color=#ffff00]This extension will automatically download and install the [/color][url=https://github.com/microsoftenator2022/MicroPatches]MicroPatches [/url][color=#ffff00]mod. This is required to fix bugs in the game's built-in mod manager. You will also receive notifications when new versions are available to download.[/color]
[color=#f9cb9c]Includes Load Order support for Owlcat mods! Mod names are written to the "OwlcatModificationManagerSettings.json" file automatically![/color][/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]MicroPatches mods with a "MicroPatches.dll" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\UnityModManager" folder.[/*]
[*]Modfinder is recognised by a "ModFinder.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Arcemi Save Editor is recognised by an "Arcemi Save Game Editor.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Portrait Manager is recognised by a "Portrait Manager Owlcat.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Owlcat mods with an "owlcatmodificationmanifest.json" file, an "Assemblies", "Blueprints", "Bundles" or "Localization" folder and a ".dll" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Modifications" folder.[/*]
[*]Plugin (UnityModManager) mods with a ".dll" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\UnityModManager" folder.[/*]
[*]Portraits mods with a "fulllength.png", "medium.png" or "small.png" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Portraits" folder.[/*]
[*]Save mods with a ".zks" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Saved Games" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Xbox - Note that Portrait mods don't work on the Xbox version[/*]
[*]Installs Owlcat mods with "OwlcatModificationManifest.json" file and "Assemblies/BluePrints/Bundles/Localization" folders to individual subfolders in "...&#92;Modifications".[/*]
[*]Custom Portraits mods are installed to "...&#92;Portraits". [color=#f9cb9c]NOTE: Portrait mods are NOT supported on the Xbox version.[/color] This is a limitation of the game, and cannot be fixed by the extension author.[/*]
[*]Modfinder, Portrait Manager, and Arcemi Save Editor can be installed with Vortex and launched using the included tools.[/*]
[*]All other mods are installed to "%userprofile%&#92;AppData&#92;LocalLow&#92;Owlcat Games&#92;Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader" with a fallback notification.[/*]
[*]Mods that need to be installed to the game's installation folder must be installed manually. This is to prevent "splitting" the installation locations across mutliple partitions and disabling hardlinks for many users.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

MicroPatches:

Recognised when the archive contains a "MicroPatches.dll" file.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\UnityModManager"

========================================================================

Modfinder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ModFinder.exe" file.

========================================================================

Arcemi Save Editor:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Arcemi Save Game Editor.exe" file.

========================================================================

Portrait Manager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Portrait Manager Owlcat.exe" file.

========================================================================

Owlcat Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "owlcatmodificationmanifest.json" file, a "Assemblies", "Blueprints", "Bundles" or "Localization" folder and a ".dll" file.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Modifications"

========================================================================

Plugin (UnityModManager):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" file.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\UnityModManager"

========================================================================

Portraits:

Recognised when the archive contains a "fulllength.png", "medium.png" or "small.png" file.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Portraits"

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".zks" extension.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader\Saved Games"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Owlcat Games\Warhammer 40000 Rogue Trader"

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

